Pomelo v2 phone tools on top of the v1 series.

Volume keys scroll the page unless a text field, fullscreen video, or
picture-in-picture has focus. More tools gains float video, page media, an
ad-blocker toggle, a volume-key toggle, userscripts, and customize menu.
Customize menu hides a fixed set of overflow ids.

Page media lists video and audio addresses seen by a request throttle plus
video/audio elements. A tap starts Android DownloadManager.

The ad blocker is an original host-suffix throttle. The list is not EasyList,
AdGuard, or any GPL engine. Main-frame navigations are not blocked. Userscripts
saved in the browser run on http(s) pages after load. An extension that
declares the userScripts permission is allowed until that pref is turned off,
so a Tampermonkey-style extension can register scripts.

